<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#061d3c"><title>A Perfectly Reasonable Idea | The Little Mini Who Wouldn’t Quit | PeterHamRN.com</title><meta name="description" content="The true story of a 2012 Mac mini resurrection, with a practical companion manual for Mac computers."><link rel="canonical" href="https://peterhamrn.com/little-mini/story/a-perfectly-reasonable-idea/"><meta property="og:title" content="A Perfectly Reasonable Idea | The Little Mini Who Wouldn’t Quit | PeterHamRN.com"><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:url" content="https://peterhamrn.com/little-mini/story/a-perfectly-reasonable-idea/"><meta property="og:site_name" content="PeterHamRN.com"><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/peterhamrn-logo.svg"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/little-mini.css"></head><body><a href="#main" class="skip">Skip to content</a><header><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/peterhamrn-logo.svg" alt="">PeterHamRN<b>.com</b></a><div class="links"><a href="/#top">Home</a><a href="/#projects">Projects</a><a href="/apps-automations.html">Apps</a><a href="/#journey">Journey</a><a href="/resources.html">Resources</a><a href="/classes/">Classes</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a></div><button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mini-mobile-nav">Menu</button></nav><div class="mobile-menu" id="mini-mobile-nav"><a href="/#top">Home</a><a href="/#projects">Projects</a><a href="/apps-automations.html">Apps</a><a href="/#journey">Journey</a><a href="/resources.html">Resources</a><a href="/classes/">Classes</a><a href="/contact">Contact</a></div></div></header><main id="main" class="wrap"><article class="reader"><p><a href="/little-mini/">← Little Mini project home</a></p><p class="publication-title">The Little Mini Who Wouldn’t Quit</p><p class="eyebrow" style="color:#0b62bf">Chapter 3</p><h1>A Perfectly Reasonable Idea</h1><p class="muted">Published <time datetime="2026-10-11">October 11, 2026</time> · <a href="/tools/little-mini/manuscripts/story-chapter-03.md" download>Download original Markdown</a></p><div class="manuscript"><h1>Do You Think This Project Is Overkill?</h1><h2>The Little Mini Who Wouldn&#39;t Quit</h2><p><em>One tiny screw. One forgotten computer. An entirely unreasonable solution.</em></p><h3>Chapter 3 — A Perfectly Reasonable Idea</h3><p>The plan was straightforward.</p><p>The Mac mini would live in the garage. Its Wi-Fi would connect to the Vantrue camera, while a separate network connection would keep it accessible from the house.</p><p>The videos would be stored on the Mini and shared with my MacBook Air, iPad, and iPhone.</p><p>Eventually, the process might even become automatic.</p><p>A fourteen-year-old computer doing a useful job instead of taking up shelf space.</p><p>What could possibly go wrong?</p><p>Well, first we needed an operating system.</p><p>The Mini was old enough that modern macOS versions weren&#39;t an option. We settled on macOS Catalina, released in 2019.</p><p>For perspective, Catalina came out before ChatGPT existed.</p><p>So there we were: a 2012 computer, a 2019 operating system, and an AI assistant introduced to the world in 2022.</p><p>The computer was the oldest member of the team.</p><p>As events unfolded, it wasn&#39;t always clear which member had the most experience.</p></div><div class="reading-navigation"><nav class="chapter-nav story-track" aria-label="Humorous story chapter navigation"><h2>Humorous story</h2><a class="chapter-previous" rel="prev" href="/little-mini/story/the-little-computer-on-death-row/">← Previous Chapter<span>2. The Little Computer on Death Row</span></a><p class="chapter-coming-soon">More chapters coming soon</p></nav><aside class="related companion-reading"><h2>C